{"agent":"recover-5g","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The harness answer path treats a missing `options` key as a crash, while `payload` and `verify` in the same change treat it as free text (`row.get(\"options\") or []` / `row.get(\"options\")`). A question ask with no `options` key (the free-text shape this payload documents: no preset choices, person types the answer) reaches `if row[\"options\"]:` and raises KeyError before `E.answer`, so the ask stays unreachable through the harness channel the bugfix claims to open.","digest":"cddf8a24953c93c3","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:489","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:489"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Multiple-choice questions record `hit.answer` as the outcome with no membership check against `row[\"options\"]`. The same `hit.answer` is arbitrary tool text on the free-text branch, so the scanner does not restrict it to presets. Given options `[\"red\", \"blue\"]` and a transcript answer `\"green\"` (or any other string) for that surfaced question, attest closes the ask with outcome `\"green\"` instead of refusing a label that was not offered.","digest":"7faee277db4905d9","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:490","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:490"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21857,"diff_sha":"a12a2dce7336804337031cc2b6da1e3c6e29fc09572f81923634c33771554745","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-question-ask-unreachable","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":106.5,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"cb90098e0f86a2da","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-question-ask-unreachable.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20