{"agent":"recover-5g","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"A question with no preset options still has no answerable surface. `payload` builds `{\"questions\":[{\"question\":...,\"header\":\"Question\",\"multiSelect\":false}]}` and omits `options`. AskUserQuestion only accepts a multiple-choice input of 2–4 `{label, description}` options (the approval branch always emits that shape, and the agent must send this payload unaltered). Given a waiting question whose `options` is missing or `[]`, the tool rejects the input, so the person cannot type the free-text answer this branch claims to record, and `attest` never sees a transcript hit. The same builder also emits 1 or 5+ options unchanged, which the tool likewise rejects.","digest":"5df698aa7c1ef924","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:payload","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:payload"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Free-text re-check reads the wrong field. `attest` stores the typed reply via `E.answer(..., text=hit.answer)` and sets `outcome` to `E.ANSWERED_WORD`, but the new question branch of `verify` requires `h.answer == row.get(\"answer\")`. Given a free-text question whose transcript answer is `\"ship the patch\"` and whose row stores that string under `text` (or only as the answer argument) with `answer` unset, `verify` returns False and a recorded harness answer fails the level check. Multiple-choice is also unchecked: `attest` sets `outcome = hit.answer` with no membership test, so a transcript label that is not in `row[\"options\"]` is recorded and then accepted by `verify`.","digest":"267bfbe3a76debbd","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:verify","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:verify"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21857,"diff_sha":"a12a2dce7336804337031cc2b6da1e